## Raised metal, recessed color

Soft enamel pins combine raised metal outlines with recessed enamel fields, creating a tactile surface and clear color separation. They suit brand logos, team mascots, trading pins and event merchandise where bold color and an accessible custom format matter.

## Color and finish choices

The artwork is translated into a custom die, then formed in metal and plated before the recessed areas are filled and cured. Pantone color references help coordinate the enamel with your identity. Glitter, glow-in-the-dark and translucent effects can be considered where they support the design.

Use strong outlines and readable color areas rather than crowding the pin with tiny details. A few well-chosen colors keep the main image clear; larger formats offer more room for fine lettering and complex artwork.

## Soft enamel or a smooth finish?

Choose soft enamel when you want visible depth between the metal and color. A polished imitation hard enamel pin offers a smoother surface, while a die-struck pin keeps the design entirely in metal. Backings, backing cards and presentation boxes complete the piece for retail, recognition or collecting.

## Plan your order

The minimum order is 50 pieces, with typical production of 7-15 business days excluding shipping. Share the logo, preferred dimensions, color references, quantity and delivery date so the artwork, finish and packaging can be reviewed together.
